    <projectUrl>https://infosys.beckhoff.com/content/1033/tc3_ads_intro/index.html</projectUrl>
    <description>ADS (TCP) Router implementation.
			This package can be used for ADS router functionality on targets that doesn't run TwinCAT Installations to communicate to local and remote ADS targets.</description>
    <releaseNotes>### 7.0.314
Fix: The managed AMS/TCP router reuses its established remote connection for targets whose AmsNetId does not end in 1.1 (SubNet targets, e.g. a.b.c.d.2.1) again. Since 7.0.147 the connection registry used a different key for adding and for looking up a connection, so a new TCP connection was opened for every single request to such a target, which surfaced as ClientSyncTimeOut from the second request onwards, #323440
### 7.0.286
Fix: The managed AMS/TCP router now rejects AMS/TCP frames whose declared body size (TcpHeader.cbSize) exceeds 64 MiB before allocating the receive buffer, and closes the connection. This prevents a memory-exhaustion denial-of-service where a crafted 6-byte header forced an arbitrarily large allocation.
### 7.0.60
Enh: AmsRouter not using app local UnixSocket path as fallback anymore.
Enh: Using LoopbackConnection as fallback, when no UnixSocket path is specified by configuration.
### 7.0.36
Breaking Change: Removes .NET6 as Dependency (out-of-support)
### 7.0
Enh: Supports internal communication via UnixSockets or TCP/IP Loopback
Enh: TargetFramework dependencies changed to net8.0, net6.0, netstandard2.0</releaseNotes>
